{"id": "unknown-2026-11-23-006", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Honduras starts paying solar prosumers for excess power", "content": "<p>Honduras has begun compensating solar self-consumption customers for surplus electricity exported to the distribution grid, with the Zamorano University campus becoming the first eligible user under tariffs of $92.50/MWh to $111.27/MWh.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/honduras-starts-paying-solar-prosumers-for-excess-power/\">Honduras starts paying solar prosumers for excess power</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/honduras-starts-paying-solar-prosumers-for-excess-power/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-23-007", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["ramp up"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Lebanon looks to ramp up solar, storage deployments", "content": "<p>Lebanon is working towards adding at least 3 GW of electricity generation capacity in the coming years, most of which is expected to come from solar and wind, alongside battery energy storage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/lebanon-looks-to-ramp-up-solar-storage-deployments/\">Lebanon looks to ramp up solar, storage deployments</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/lebanon-looks-to-ramp-up-solar-storage-deployments/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-23-008", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Wind-driven spray system cools, cleans solar panels", "content": "<p>Researchers have developed a water spray system that cools and cleans PV modules using a wind turbine coupled directly to a mechanical pump. In rooftop tests, the system lowered cell temperature by up to 26.7 C and increased peak power output by 18.6%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/wind-driven-spray-system-cools-cleans-solar-panels/\">Wind-driven spray system cools, cleans solar panels</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glo", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/wind-driven-spray-system-cools-cleans-solar-panels/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-23-009", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Europe turns negative electricity prices into a flexibility signal", "content": "<p>Negative wholesale power prices are a useful investment signal for batteries and demand response in Europe only where subsidy design and grid bottlenecks are not distorting them, says a new Eurelectric report.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/europe-turns-negative-electricity-prices-into-a-flexibility-signal/\">Europe turns negative electricity prices into a flexibility signal</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/europe-turns-negative-electricity-prices-into-a-flexibility-signal/", "type": "rss"}]}
