{"id": "unknown-2026-11-23-011", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Hydrogen shifts summer solar to winter in Japanese apartment building", "content": "<p>Japanese contractor Takenaka has run a hydrogen system that stores surplus summer solar power for winter use in an apartment block in central Japan for a full year and says it worked as planned, though it has published no performance data.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/hydrogen-shifts-summer-solar-to-winter-in-japanese-apartment-building/\">Hydrogen shifts summer solar to winter in Japanese apartment building</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magaz", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/23/hydrogen-shifts-summer-solar-to-winter-in-japanese-apartment-building/", "type": "rss"}]}
